A||N||8||bHooper||installing a new steering rack.||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||11-13-2000||10:31 AM||||as part of my suspension rebuild, i bought a new steering rack.  i plan on putting this in tonight.<P>has anyone ever done this b4?  is there a good trick to getting the steering wheel and everything to line up nicely?<P>it didn't come with a lot of directions!<P>thanks!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alien.gif">  <BR>We are not alone!||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||11-13-2000||03:20 PM||||is there any difficulty getting it "centered"?  <P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alien.gif">  <BR>We are not alone!||||reg||1
Z||000002||gixxer||11-13-2000||06:01 PM||||No problem centering it on MY car. If you've made a note of approx. what the angle of the pinch bolt is on the steering rack at the staight ahead position, you'll have no problem assembling it. The various pinch bolt couplings have flats on them to make your life easier. I also found it useful to disconnect the U-Joint shaft at the column also.<BR>Have fun.. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||11-13-2000||07:00 PM||||Get it aligned.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||11-13-2000||07:17 PM||||it goes without saying, that i would have the car aligned  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>gixxer, not sure what you mean by "flats"<P>||||reg||14
Z||000005||theogre||11-13-2000||07:28 PM||||If I remember right the shaft on the rack is made so it only fits one way. I forget wether its a flat spot on the shaft or an od spline. A long as the wheels are straight you can't get it wrong.<P>The U joint under the dash definatly fits only one way. That one is keyed to the column shaft and you must take out the bolt to separate the 2.||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||11-13-2000||08:43 PM||||Right, the input shaft to the rack is flat on one side so it only goes in one way. It sounds like you were hoping to get the rack in without an alignment (steering wheel straight). ||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||11-13-2000||09:49 PM||||nononono, i know the car  is going to need an alignment.  i jsut dint want to put the sucker together and have 1/4 to 1/2 a turn in either direction.<P>i think i understand everything now.<P>thanks!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||11-13-2000||11:22 PM||||Just center steering wheel before you install it. Make sure you count the outer tie-rod end turns before you remove them and then center the rack and put the tie-rod on the same number of turns. It will be close enough to get down to the shop. ||||reg||1
